# ColQwen2.5 service configuration - generated by setup-colqwen.sh
# Generated: ${GENERATED_DATE}
#
# This file is the single configuration source for the generated project.
# Edit values, then apply them with:
#   docker compose build && docker compose up -d

# NVIDIA NGC PyTorch base image tag (nvcr.io/nvidia/pytorch:<tag>).
# The tag must match BOTH the host driver (its CUDA version) and the torch
# pin of the colpali-engine version below. No validation takes place - you
# are responsible for picking a compatible tag.
# Tested combination (DGX Spark GB10, driver 580.x / CUDA 13.0):
#   25.10-py3 (torch 2.9, CUDA 13.0.2) + colpali-engine 0.3.13
NGC_PYTORCH_TAG=${NGC_PYTORCH_TAG}

# colpali-engine version installed into the image (pip, exact pin).
# Coupled to the transformers generation it is built for: 0.3.13 is the last
# release on transformers 4.x, whose checkpoint layout matches the vidore
# ColQwen2.5 models. 0.3.14+ expect transformers 5.x, which renames the
# model keys (model.* -> language_model.*) and - as of 0.3.17/5.14 -
# silently DROPS the LoRA adapter weights of vidore/colqwen2.5-v0.2 and
# cannot load its processor offline.
# NOTE: colpali-engine is installed with --no-deps (its torch pin would make
# pip replace the NGC CUDA torch); its companion libraries (transformers,
# peft, accelerate) are pinned in the Dockerfile and must be kept in sync
# with this version.
COLPALI_VERSION=${COLPALI_VERSION}

# Host directory containing the models - typically the Hugging Face cache
# (with models under hub/models--vidore--colqwen2.5-v0.2/...), populated via
# 'hf download'. Mounted read-only at the IDENTICAL path in the container so
# absolute base-model paths in adapter_config.json resolve; HF_HOME points
# at it. Models are never downloaded - place them here yourself.
COLQWEN_MODEL_DIR=${COLQWEN_MODEL_DIR}

# Model the service loads at startup. Either a HF model ID resolved offline
# from the mounted cache:
#   COLQWEN_MODEL=vidore/colqwen2.5-v0.2
# or an absolute path to a model directory inside COLQWEN_MODEL_DIR:
#   COLQWEN_MODEL=/srv/models/colqwen2.5-v0.2
COLQWEN_MODEL=${COLQWEN_MODEL}

# Host port mapped to the service (container port 8000).
COLQWEN_PORT=${COLQWEN_PORT}

# Host address the port is published on. Default 127.0.0.1 - the service is
# unauthenticated, and anything else exposes /embed/queries and /embed/images
# to the network. Note that ufw does NOT protect this: Docker's published-port
# DNAT rules run ahead of ufw's filter chains, so a default-deny policy will
# not close a 0.0.0.0-published port.
#
# Keep this on loopback when the only caller is a process on the host itself
# (e.g. a llama-swap "colqwen" model proxying to 127.0.0.1:${COLQWEN_PORT}).
# Set 0.0.0.0 only behind a reverse proxy that does the authentication.
COLQWEN_BIND=${COLQWEN_BIND}
